<div class="page">

  <div class="series-label">Likutay Halachos &mdash; Yoreh Day&lsquo;ah</div>
  <h1>Hilchos Avadim</h1>
  <h2>Halachah Beis</h2>
  <h3>Inyan Milas Avadim &mdash; The Matter of the Circumcision of Slaves</h3>
  <hr class="rule">

  <!-- SECTION 1 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">1</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      According to the Talmudic saying: &ldquo;Rabbi Akiva said: When you reach the stones of
      pure marble, do not say &lsquo;water, water!&rsquo; as it is written,
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&lsquo;one who speaks falsehood shall not stand before My eyes&rsquo;</em></span>&rdquo;
      &mdash; see the words of Rabbeinu, of blessed memory, may I be an atonement for his resting place,
      where this entire teaching is explained well
      <span class="editorial-note">((Siman 51))</span>.
    </p>
    <p>
      And the general principle is this: if one desires that
      <em>post-creation be as pre-creation</em> &mdash; that Father and Son be as one
      (<span class="aramaic">av u-ven ka-chada</span>), that everything be entirely one,
      entirely good &mdash; one must be vigilant against falsehood. For through truth, the
      <span class="key-term">hashgachah</span> [Divine providence] of the Blessed One rests
      upon us, and then all is one &mdash; for through His blessed providence,
      post-creation is included within pre-creation, in the aspect of Father and Son as one.
      But through falsehood, He removes His blessed providence, as it is written:
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;one who speaks falsehood shall not stand before My eyes&rdquo;</em></span>
      <span class="verse-source">[Tehillim 101:7]</span>. For truth is one, but falsehood is
      distant from oneness &mdash; in the aspect of <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;they sought
      many calculations&rdquo;</em></span> &mdash; and the primary grip of falsehood, which is the
      evil, which is the impurity, comes from distance from the One. For immediately after
      creation, the aspect of &ldquo;two&rdquo; began &mdash; namely, creation and pre-creation
      &mdash; and from there the chain of falsehood, which is the evil, descended. But before
      creation, all was entirely good, entirely holy &mdash; even the term &ldquo;purity&rdquo;
      was not applicable there, for purity begins only after creation, since purity implies
      that there is impurity; it is the aspect of the side of Levi, the side of the left, from
      which the grip of the <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span> [the Other Side], which
      is falsehood, descends. And therefore one can ascend from impurity to purity, for the
      primary chain of the grip of impurity is from the aspect of purity itself &mdash; in the
      aspect of <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;and you shall purify the sons of Levi&rdquo;</em></span>
      &mdash; see there the full matter, for it is exceedingly deep.
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 2 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">2</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">milas avadim</span>
      [circumcision of slaves]. For the <span class="key-term">orlah</span>, which is the
      <span class="key-term">zuhamas ha-nachash</span> [the filth of the serpent], is in the
      aspect of falsehood &mdash; which is the evil, which is the impurity, the aspect of
      the <span class="key-term">zuhamas ha-nachash</span>, as is known. For when the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> is removed, he is then in the aspect of the
      <span class="key-term">chosam emes</span> [seal of truth], the aspect of the
      <span class="key-term">os emes</span> [sign of truth], which is the aspect of the
      holy <span class="key-term">bris</span> [covenant] &mdash; as the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> that covers over the <span class="key-term">bris</span>,
      which is in the aspect of falsehood, in the aspect of
      <span class="aramaic">m&rsquo;shakker b&rsquo;chosamah d&rsquo;malka</span>
      [forging the king&rsquo;s seal], is removed from him. For the primary
      <span class="key-term">tzelem Elokim</span> [image of God], the
      <span class="aramaic">tzelem d&rsquo;mus tavniso</span> [likeness of His form], as it were,
      is a circumcised man who is sealed with the seal of truth. But when the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> covers over the <span class="key-term">bris</span>,
      it is in the aspect of falsehood &mdash; for it is not the image of a human being at all,
      since as long as the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> is upon him he is entirely
      blemished, as Rashi explains on the verse
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;hishalech l&rsquo;fanai v&rsquo;heyai tamim&rdquo;</em></span>
      [&ldquo;Walk before Me and be wholesome&rdquo;] &mdash; see there. Thus the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> is in the aspect of falsehood literally, for it
      misrepresents the form of the human being; for in truth the <span class="key-term">orlah</span>
      is not from the form of the human being at all, and it clings to the person through utter
      falsehood &mdash; it appears as though it is part of the body, yet in truth it is complete
      falsehood, for it is not the image of a human being, since the primary form of man, the
      <span class="key-term">tzelem Elokim</span>, is when one is sealed with the holy
      <span class="key-term">bris</span> with the seal of the sign of truth, through the removal
      of the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> &mdash; for then one is called <em>tamim</em>
      [wholesome], as above. And so it is explained in many places that the guarding of the
      <span class="key-term">bris</span>, which is the aspect of the mitzvah of milah, is the
      aspect of truth, the aspect of <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;kulah zera emes&rdquo;</em></span>
      [&ldquo;all of her seed is truth&rdquo;] <span class="verse-source">((Yirmiyahu 2))</span>.
      And conversely, blemishing the <span class="key-term">bris</span> in the aspect of
      <span class="key-term">orlah d&rsquo;chafya al bris</span> [the foreskin that covers the
      covenant] is in the aspect of falsehood &mdash; which is the
      <span class="key-term">zuhamas ha-nachash</span>. And this is the aspect of the slave, who
      is cursed, in the aspect of <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;arur Kenaan eved avadim&rdquo;</span>
      [cursed is Canaan, a slave of slaves], who is the seed of Cham, in the aspect of blemishing
      the <span class="key-term">bris</span>, the <span class="key-term">zuhamas ha-nachash</span>,
      of whom it is said: <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;arur atah&rdquo;</span> [cursed are you],
      as is cited. It is thus found that the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> &mdash; which is
      the aspect of falsehood, the <span class="key-term">zuhamas ha-nachash</span> &mdash; is
      the aspect of the slave who is cursed, as above. For the slave is in the aspect of
      falsehood, whose grip comes from the chain of post-creation. For through falsehood,
      post-creation is not included within pre-creation, as above &mdash; as it is written,
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;one who speaks falsehood shall not stand before My eyes&rdquo;</em></span>
      <span class="verse-source">((Tehillim 101))</span> &mdash; and then Father and Son are not
      as one, as it were, as above. And then one falls into bondage, God forbid, for the slave
      is the opposite of the son &mdash; when one is in the aspect of son, post-creation is
      included within pre-creation in the aspect of Father and Son as one, Father and Son
      precisely, for the son is drawn from the mind of the father and therefore when he is in
      the aspect of son, Father and Son are automatically as one, and post-creation is included
      within pre-creation. But through falsehood, God forbid, there is no Father and Son as one,
      and then one is in the aspect of slave, for the slave is distant from the master and is not
      in the aspect of oneness with the master. Thus the slave is in the aspect of falsehood,
      in the aspect of <span class="key-term">orlah</span>, in the aspect of distance from
      oneness. For the primary aspect of being entirely one &mdash; that post-creation be as
      pre-creation &mdash; is only in the aspect of son, the aspect of Father and Son as one,
      Father and Son precisely, as above. And so it is hinted at in the words of Rabbeinu, of
      blessed memory, in another place
      <span class="editorial-note">((Siman 117))</span>, that the slave is in the aspect of
      falsehood which is the <span class="key-term">zuhamas ha-nachash</span> &mdash; see there.
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 3 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">3</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And therefore the Torah commanded to circumcise the son &mdash; to remove the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> which is falsehood &mdash; in order that His blessed
      providence be drawn upon us, so that post-creation be as pre-creation, in the aspect of
      Father and Son as one, in the aspect of all being one. For this is the primary purpose of
      our service and the primary goal: to merit that post-creation be included within
      pre-creation. For the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> is in the aspect of
      <span class="aramaic">ananin d&rsquo;mechasyan al ainin</span> [clouds that cover the eyes]
      &mdash; and thereby His blessed providence does not rest upon him, for the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> is the blemishing of the <span class="key-term">bris</span>,
      which is the blemishing of the eyes, as is cited. But when the
      <span class="key-term">orlah d&rsquo;chafya al bris</span> is removed, thereby the clouds
      that cover the eyes are removed, and His blessed providence rests upon us, and thereby
      Father and Son are as one &mdash; for thereby one exits from the aspect of slave, which is
      the aspect of falsehood, to the aspect of son, and then all is one, Father and Son as one,
      as above.
    </p>
    <p>
      And therefore the primary obligation is upon the father to circumcise his son &mdash; for
      pre-creation and post-creation is also in the aspect of father and son, as is explained in
      the teaching above, for He blessed be He is called Father, and the totality of creation is
      called son &mdash; from the moment creation emerged from potential to actual, a grip was
      formed for falsehood, which is the <span class="key-term">orlah</span>, and we must remove
      the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> so that Father and Son be as one, as above. And by
      the fact that the father himself circumcises his son, through this &mdash; by the arousal
      from below awakening the arousal from above
      (<span class="aramaic">b&rsquo;it&rsquo;arusa d&rsquo;litata it&rsquo;ar l&rsquo;eila</span>)
      &mdash; He blessed be He, Who is our Father, also removes the <span class="key-term">orlah</span>
      which is falsehood from the totality of creation, so that Father and Son be as one, as above.
      It is thus found that the primary purpose of the mitzvah of milah is to eradicate the
      falsehood which is the <span class="key-term">orlah</span>, which is the aspect of slave,
      which is the evil and the impurity &mdash; in order that they be in the aspect of the seal
      of the sign of truth, so that post-creation be as pre-creation, Father and Son as one,
      as above.
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 4 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">4</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And therefore the Torah commanded to circumcise the slave &mdash; in order to subdue and
      nullify the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> at its root, which is the aspect of slave,
      which is the opposite of son: the aspect of post-creation when it is not included, God
      forbid, within pre-creation, through the grip of falsehood which takes hold of it &mdash;
      for then creation is not in the aspect of son but in the aspect of slave, and there is where
      the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> takes hold, which is the aspect of falsehood, as
      above. And therefore when one circumcises the slave and removes the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> from him, thereby the <span class="key-term">orlah</span>
      is subdued in its place and at its root &mdash; for there is its place, in the aspect of
      slave, as above. And then, when the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> is subdued and
      removed from the slave, the slave too can become included within the aspect of son, for the
      primary bondage is due to the grip of falsehood, through which he is distanced from oneness,
      and then he is not in the aspect of son but in the aspect of slave. But when the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span>, which is falsehood, is removed, the slave is included
      within son, and all becomes one.
    </p>
    <p>
      For it is stated in the holy Zohar in <span class="key-term">Ra&rsquo;aya Mehaimna</span>
      [the Faithful Shepherd], Parashas Behar, that every one of Israel must serve the Blessed One
      in two aspects: in the aspect of son and in the aspect of slave. And this is the primary
      perfection &mdash; when one&rsquo;s service is comprised of both aspects, son and slave
      &mdash; see there. And the matter, according to the above: before creation, all was one;
      and immediately when creation emerged from potential to actual, there were immediately
      two aspects &mdash; pre-creation and post-creation &mdash; and from there descended the
      grip of the <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span>, which is falsehood. And this is
      the aspect of right and left, son and slave. For pre-creation is in the aspect of
      <span class="aramaic">kola yemina</span> [all is right], for
      <span class="aramaic">leis s&rsquo;mala tamman</span> [there is no left there], as above.
      And the totality of creation, compared to pre-creation, is in the aspect of left, as is
      understood from Rabbeinu&rsquo;s words in the above teaching. And from this descended all
      the aspects of right and left found everywhere, for they all descended from these two
      aspects: son, which is when post-creation is included within pre-creation in the aspect
      of Father and Son as one; and slave, which is when it is not included, God forbid, as above.
    </p>
    <p>
      And the entire purpose of our service is to include the left within the right &mdash; and
      each person, according to how he merits through his service to subdue the
      <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span> that grips the side of the left, so that the
      left be included within the right &mdash; correspondingly and proportionally, post-creation
      is included within pre-creation for him, which is the ultimate goal of all our service,
      as above. And therefore one must serve the Blessed One in both aspects: in the aspect of
      son and in the aspect of slave, which are the aspects of right and left &mdash; so that the
      left be included within the right, and post-creation within pre-creation, as above. And this
      is the aspect of <span class="key-term">milas avadim</span>, for through circumcising the
      slave and removing from him the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> which is falsehood,
      whose primary grip is in the aspect of slave, thereby slave is included within son, left
      within right &mdash; for even though he remains a slave, this is nonetheless the primary
      service: that the slave, the aspect of left, be included within the right, in the aspect
      of son. And therefore afterwards he is obligated in the commandments that a woman is
      obligated in, for he is in the aspect of left, the aspect of
      <span class="key-term">ishah</span> &mdash; and through removing the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> from him, he can thereby be included within the left
      of holiness, and then the left of holiness is included within the right, as is known &mdash;
      for this is the primary service everywhere: wherever there is left and right, to subdue
      the evil that grips the left, and thereby the left is included within the right, and through
      this post-creation is included within pre-creation, as above. Also, the slave is the
      master&rsquo;s <span class="key-term">miknos kaspo</span> [monetary acquisition], which is
      in the aspect of left, in the aspect of
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;uvism&rsquo;olah osher&rdquo;</em></span>
      [&ldquo;and in her left, riches&rdquo;] <span class="verse-source">((Mishlai 3))</span>.
      And through subduing the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> that grips the aspect of his
      wealth, which is itself the aspect of slave as above, thereby the left is included within
      the right, and through this post-creation is included within pre-creation &mdash; which
      is the ultimate purpose of all our service, as above.
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 5 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">5</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of what is forbidden: to emancipate the slave &mdash; as it is
      written, <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;and you shall bequeath them to your children
      after you&hellip; you shall work them forever&rdquo;</em></span>. For this work and
      this refinement &mdash; to subdue and nullify the evil gripping the totality of creation
      so that post-creation be included within pre-creation &mdash; this refinement we must
      perform all our days, in every generation, until the end &mdash; until the spirit of
      impurity passes entirely from the earth. And then everything will truly be nullified and
      return to its root, and all will be one as before creation. But now, as long as the Blessed
      One desires the continued existence of the world, we must pursue all our service in the
      aspect of <span class="key-term">ratzo va-shov</span> [running and returning] &mdash;
      that the totality of creation be included within pre-creation, and yet the existence of
      creation continue and not be nullified entirely, God forbid &mdash; for the Blessed One
      desires the continued existence of the world. And therefore the primary service is to
      refine, elevate, and include the left within the right, and yet the existence of the left
      remain &mdash; for the side of the left is the sustaining of the world, as is known.
    </p>
    <p>
      And therefore it is forbidden to emancipate the slave &mdash; so as not to nullify the
      aspect of the left entirely before its time. Rather, one should circumcise him, to eradicate
      the utterly evil <span class="key-term">orlah</span> from him, so that afterwards, through
      the Israelite working him, the good within him can be refined and the left included within
      the right, slave within son &mdash; but not to emancipate him entirely, for then one is
      nullifying the aspect of the left entirely before its time. For one is not permitted to
      nullify the aspect of the left entirely until the end. And this is the verse:
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;and you shall bequeath them to your children&rdquo;</em></span>
      &mdash; <em>to your children</em> precisely. For the slave must serve <em>the son</em>,
      so that the slave be included within son, the left within the right &mdash; so that through
      this, post-creation be included within pre-creation, as above. For the more that the left
      is included within the right, correspondingly post-creation is included within pre-creation,
      as above.
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 6 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">6</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">S&rsquo;firas ha-Omer</span> and
      <span class="key-term">Shavuos</span>. For it is stated that during the
      <span class="key-term">S&rsquo;firah</span> one ascends from impurity to purity through
      counting the <span class="key-term">Omer</span> &mdash; for then we purify ourselves from
      the impurity of Egypt in order to merit receiving the Torah on Shavuos. And at first
      glance this is puzzling: how does counting the days purify us? What does counting days have
      to do with purity? But according to the above, the matter of the counting is well explained.
    </p>
    <p>
      For the primary grip of the <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span> &mdash; which is
      falsehood, which is the evil and the impurity &mdash; its primary grip is in the aspect of
      number (<span class="key-term">mispar</span>). For before creation, all was one, entirely
      good, and there in the aspect of oneness there is certainly no concept of number at all
      &mdash; as one says: &ldquo;before One, what do you count?&rdquo; And immediately when the
      Blessed One brought creation forth from potential to actual, the aspect of number began
      immediately, for immediately there were two aspects, as Rabbeinu wrote in the above
      teaching. And when there are two aspects, number is applicable, and from there the chain
      descended until the grip of the <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span>, which is the
      aspect of <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;many calculations&rdquo;</em></span> &mdash;
      that through the multiplication of number and the distancing from oneness, the chain
      descended to the aspect of many calculations, which is the grip of the
      <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span>, which is the aspect of falsehood, which is
      distant from oneness, as above. It is thus found that the primary grip of the
      <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span>, which is falsehood, which is impurity, is
      from the aspect of number. And the root of number in holiness, before it chains down to
      impurity &mdash; that is, immediately after creation, when the aspect of number first came
      into being &mdash; is still in holiness. This is the aspect of purity explained in the
      above teaching &mdash; namely, immediately after creation when the aspect of &ldquo;two&rdquo;
      arose, the aspect of number. This is an impression (<span class="key-term">roshem</span>)
      that will eventually chain down until impurity arises &mdash; yet before it chains down, it
      is in the aspect of purity, as is explained there.
    </p>
    <p>
      And therefore whoever wishes to emerge from impurity must ascend to the aspect of purity,
      for purity, which is the aspect of post-creation immediately, the aspect of number, is the
      root of impurity &mdash; and therefore precisely through it one ascends from impurity to
      purity, as explained well in the above teaching. And therefore, after we merited to leave
      Egypt from bondage to freedom &mdash; for Egypt is from the seed of Cham, which is the
      aspect of blemishing the <span class="key-term">bris</span>, the
      <span class="key-term">zuhamas ha-nachash</span>, the aspect of slave of slaves &mdash;
      and therefore after we left there from bondage to freedom and we must purify ourselves from
      the impurity of Egypt, to ascend from impurity to purity, the Blessed One therefore
      commanded us to count <span class="key-term">S&rsquo;firas ha-Omer</span>. For precisely
      through the aspect of number, which is the root of the grip of impurity, precisely thereby
      does one ascend from impurity to purity, for number in holiness is in the aspect of purity,
      which purifies from all impurities since from there comes the chain of impurity, as above
      &mdash; as it is written: <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;and you shall be purified
      from all your impurities&rdquo;</em></span>, as explained in the above teaching.
    </p>
    <p>
      For the number of holiness (<span class="key-term">mispar d&rsquo;kedushah</span>), which
      is the aspect of immediately post-creation &mdash; that is, a number of truth in which there
      is no falsehood, a number in holiness and purity guarded from falsehood, meaning guarded
      so that the <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span>, which is falsehood and impurity,
      does not grip it &mdash; this number, which is post-creation, is included within
      pre-creation and from the number all becomes one, as above. And therefore it is said at the
      beginning of creation: <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;vay&rsquo;hi erev vay&rsquo;hi
      voker yom echad&rdquo;</em></span> [and there was evening and there was morning, day one]
      <span class="verse-source">((Bereishis 1))</span> &mdash; and it does not say
      &ldquo;first&rdquo; (<em>rishon</em>) so that all of creation be included within the aspect
      of One, in the aspect of all being one, all being good, so that all the numbers that follow
      &mdash; all of which arose post-creation as above &mdash; should all be included and counted
      toward the aspect of One, so that all be included within the aspect of all being one. And
      therefore the holy Torah counted each day of creation, as it is written: evening and morning
      &mdash; day two, day three, etc. &mdash; so that the number, which is in the aspect of
      post-creation, be included in holiness, so that thereby all number, which is all of creation,
      be included within the aspect of One. Accordingly the Torah began the count from One, as
      above, for through the holy Torah counting the days of creation, all of creation which is
      in the aspect of number as above is included within the aspect of pre-creation, the aspect
      of all being one, as above.
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 7 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">7</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of what we find in the words of our Sages, of blessed memory,
      that one must not count Israel &mdash; for wherever there is counting, a curse rests,
      God forbid. And therefore the Torah warned that when it is necessary to know the count
      of the children of Israel, one must take from each person a half-shekel as ransom for
      his soul. And it is also stated in the holy Zohar that before the count they would bless
      Israel, and similarly afterward &mdash; all of this to guard them so that the curse that
      grips the count and the tally would not have power, God forbid, as explained in the holy
      Zohar. For certainly the primary grip of the curse &mdash; which is the aspect of
      <span class="aramaic">arur</span> [cursed], the aspect of
      <span class="aramaic">arur Kenaan</span>, <span class="aramaic">arur ha-nachash</span>
      &mdash; descends from the aspect of number and tally. And therefore it is forbidden to
      count Israel, so that the curse that grips the count not have power, God forbid &mdash; in
      the aspect of <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;they sought many calculations&rdquo;</em></span>,
      as above.
    </p>
    <p>
      And therefore they took a half-shekel per head as charity (<span class="key-term">tzedakah</span>)
      as ransom for their souls, for through charity one is saved from their grip and the
      falsehood &mdash; which is impurity, which is the curse &mdash; has no grip. For post-creation
      is included within pre-creation, all being one, as above &mdash; and all this is achieved
      through charity. For charity is the aspect of truth, the aspect of connecting truth and
      faith, and through this post-creation is included within pre-creation in the aspect of
      all being one, as above. For charity connects and binds all worlds so they are included
      in their root, in the aspect of all being one. And therefore precisely through the charity
      of a half-shekel per head, they are saved from the grip of the <span class="key-term">Sitrah
      Achara</span> through the count, for we include the count in holiness, in the aspect of
      pre-creation, in the aspect of all being one, through the charity, as above &mdash; and
      then the curse and the <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span> have no grip at all, for
      their primary grip is due to distance from oneness, as above. But when the count is connected
      to oneness &mdash; when post-creation is included within pre-creation in the aspect of all
      being one as above &mdash; they are entirely nullified and have no grip or dominion at all.
    </p>
    <p>
      And the Zohar states in the holy <span class="key-term">Idra</span>:
      <span class="aramaic">kad alin b&rsquo;chushvana, y&rsquo;havin agra</span> [when they enter
      the count, they give payment] to <span class="key-term">Atik Yomin</span> &mdash; meaning,
      when there is a count and tally and one fears lest the grip of
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;many calculations&rdquo;</em></span> take hold, God
      forbid, then one gives a half-shekel per head. And through this one connects oneself to the
      aspect of <span class="key-term">Gulgalta</span>, which is the aspect of
      <span class="key-term">Atika</span>, the aspect of truth, the aspect of
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;rosh d&rsquo;varcha emes&rdquo;</em></span>
      [&ldquo;the beginning of Your word is truth&rdquo;] <span class="verse-source">((Tehillim 119))</span>
      &mdash; which is entirely right, all one. But when all is one, they have no grip and are
      entirely nullified, as above.
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 8 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">8</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">S&rsquo;firas ha-Omer</span> &mdash; to
      ascend from impurity to purity through the counting of the Omer, which is the aspect of
      <span class="key-term">mispar d&rsquo;kedushah</span> included in its root in the aspect
      of all being one, as above. Precisely through this does one ascend from impurity to purity,
      as above. For we count the days of the Omer, and the offering of the Omer was also in this
      same aspect &mdash; that post-creation be included within pre-creation through left being
      included within right, animal within human, for the Omer of barley is animal fodder, as it
      is stated in the holy Zohar, and as cited above many times. And through waving the Omer
      before God and offering it, we thereby raise and wave the totality of creation so that it
      be included within pre-creation &mdash; through waving the Omer of barley, which is in the
      aspect of animal, the aspect of post-creation, before God, as above. And therefore
      afterwards we count the <span class="key-term">S&rsquo;firas ha-Omer</span>, seven weeks
      corresponding to the seven days of creation &mdash; in order to connect all of creation
      that was created in the seven days of creation, which is in the aspect of number, for after
      creation number begins as above &mdash; to connect it all to the Omer, which is the aspect
      of connecting post-creation to pre-creation, as is the aspect of the waving of the Omer
      of barley, as above. And precisely through this counting one ascends from impurity to
      purity, as above &mdash; and then we are purified from the filth of the bondage that was
      in Egypt, where the primary bondage was in the aspect of Cham, as above. For the primary
      filth of the aspect of slave, which is impurity, the aspect of <span class="key-term">orlah</span>,
      the aspect of blemishing the <span class="key-term">bris</span>, the aspect of the impurity
      of Egypt, the aspect of falsehood &mdash; all of it is only due to distance from oneness,
      and their grip is from the aspect of number and tally, as above. And they are sweetened at
      their root &mdash; precisely through the number of holiness that is included within the
      aspect of One, the aspect of <span class="key-term">S&rsquo;firas ha-Omer</span> &mdash;
      thereby they are sweetened at their root and their grip is nullified, for all number which
      is post-creation is included within the aspect of all being one, and then they have no grip
      at all, as above.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="editorial-note">((And see further on this matter below in Hilchos Simanei
      B&rsquo;heimah v&rsquo;Chayah T&rsquo;horah, in volume 14.))</span>
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 9 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">9</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;vilah</span> [immersion] of
      the slave &mdash; for one must raise him from impurity to purity, from the aspect of
      falsehood, the aspect of many calculations, so that he ascend to the aspect of purity from
      which their grip descends and where they are sweetened and purified, as above. And therefore
      all immersions are in the waters of a <span class="key-term">mikveh</span>, for water is
      in the aspect of pre-creation &mdash; for water preceded the world, for water is the aspect
      of <span class="key-term">Chesed</span>, the aspect of right, which is the aspect of
      pre-creation. And through entering the waters and the entire body submerging and becoming
      nullified and hidden within the water &mdash; thereby one is nullified and included within
      the aspect of pre-creation, and then he is in the aspect of all being one, as above, and
      he is purified from all impurities and ascends from them &mdash; for all impurities are
      nullified there in the aspect of all being one, for their primary grip is due to distance
      from oneness, as above. And therefore when Israel drew close to the Blessed One, they
      drew close also through milah and immersion, as above.
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 10 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">10</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ger</span> [convert] who comes to
      convert &mdash; who must also undergo milah and immersion, to subdue the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> which is the evil, which is the impurity of the nations
      (<span class="key-term">tumas ha-akum</span>), for all the nations are uncircumcised
      (<span class="key-term">areilim</span>). For the nations are in the aspect of falsehood
      and Israel is in the aspect of truth, as it is written:
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;sh&rsquo;eris Yisrael&rdquo;</em></span> [the remnant
      of Israel&hellip;] and as is cited. And therefore all the nations are called by the name of
      the <span class="key-term">orlah</span>, as above, and as our Sages said that the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> is only called by the name of the nations, for the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> is in the aspect of falsehood, the aspect of the
      impurity of the nations. And therefore the convert cannot enter the holiness of Israel
      except through milah and immersion &mdash; for through removing the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> which is falsehood, the impurity of the nations is
      thereby nullified from him, and then he becomes all one, entirely good, and then he too
      returns to the holiness of Israel, as above. And this is the aspect of the immersion, as above.
    </p>
    <p>
      And therefore the milah must precede the immersion &mdash; for first one must remove the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> which is falsehood, and only then can one merit purity
      through being included within the waters in the aspect of pre-creation. For as long as the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span>, which is falsehood, is within him, he cannot be
      included within the aspect of pre-creation, which is the aspect of immersion as above.
      Only after the filth of the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> is removed from him, and
      he is then included within the aspect of the sign of truth, can he then receive purity
      through immersion in water, through being included within the aspect of pre-creation in
      the aspect of all being one, as above. For it is impossible to be included within the
      aspect of pre-creation &mdash; that is, for post-creation to be as pre-creation, Father
      and Son as one &mdash; except through guarding against falsehood, as above. For this is the
      aspect of removing the <span class="key-term">orlah</span> which is falsehood, as above.
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 11 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">11</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">bais din</span> [court] of three that
      is required for the milah and immersion of a convert &mdash; derived by our Sages from the
      word <em>mishpat</em> [judgment] in relation to the convert: just as judgment requires
      three, so too a convert requires three. For in every judgment and adjudication, three are
      required &mdash; for judgment is to subdue falsehood and clarify truth, for this is the
      primary purpose of adjudication before judges: one litigant argues truth and one argues
      falsehood, and the judges must clarify the truth and subdue the falsehood.
    </p>
    <p>
      And therefore in every judgment and adjudication one must subdue falsehood at its root
      &mdash; that is, one must connect to the aspect of all being one, the aspect of the totality
      of creation included within pre-creation, in the aspect of Father and Son as one &mdash;
      for through this aspect, falsehood is entirely nullified and has no grip at all, since all
      is one, as above. And this aspect of the totality of post-creation included within
      pre-creation, achieved through truth &mdash; through the judges ruling true judgment
      (<span class="key-term">din emes l&rsquo;amito</span>) &mdash; this aspect is a threefold
      one, for it is comprised of three aspects which are the general sustaining of all worlds:
      the aspects of right, left, and center. For pre-creation, before creation emerged at all
      from potential to actual, is in the aspect of entirely right
      (<span class="aramaic">kola yemina</span>), for there is no left there, as above. And
      post-creation, when creation emerged from potential to actual, is in the aspect of left
      compared to pre-creation, as above. And immediately when creation emerged from potential
      to actual, an impression formed of the chain of the <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span>,
      which is evil, falsehood, and impurity, as above. And all our service is to subdue the
      falsehood, which is the <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span>, so that post-creation
      return and be included within pre-creation, that all of creation be one, as before creation
      &mdash; and then falsehood will be entirely nullified, as above. And this aspect is a
      third aspect, the aspect of center, the aspect of the decisive line
      (<span class="key-term">kav ha-makria</span>) &mdash; the aspect that even after creation,
      after creation has already emerged from potential to actual, all of creation will be included
      within pre-creation, through connecting all of creation to its root in the aspect of all
      being one through truth, as above. This aspect is the aspect of the decisive line which
      connects and joins right and left &mdash; this being the aspect of joining and including
      post-creation within pre-creation, as above.
    </p>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of the general holiness of Israel which is comprised of Kohanim,
      Levites, and Israelites, corresponding to the three Patriarchs: Avraham, Yitzchak,
      Yaakov &mdash; all of which is this threefold aspect, the aspect of right, left, and the
      decisive center, as above. And therefore when one must adjudicate judgment to expel
      falsehood and clarify truth, three judges are required, corresponding to these three aspects
      &mdash; for the <span class="key-term">bais din</span> is in the aspect of right, left,
      and the decisive center, as our Sages said: &ldquo;a court must not be evenly divided&rdquo;
      [i.e., there must always be an odd number capable of deciding]. And therefore through
      these three, who correspond to the three aspects above, post-creation is included within
      pre-creation in the aspect of all being one, and through this falsehood is subdued &mdash;
      for the primary grip of falsehood is due to its distance from oneness, and wherever the
      left is included within the right through the decisive center, correspondingly
      post-creation is included within pre-creation, as above.
    </p>
    <p>
      And therefore the convert who comes to convert &mdash; whose primary entry into the
      holiness of Israel is only through removing falsehood from him, which is the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span>, and including him within the aspect of pre-creation
      through immersion in water, through which precisely one ascends from impurity to purity and
      the aspect of all being one etc., as above &mdash; must have three present at his milah and
      immersion, as in judgment. For to take the convert out from the impurity of the nations,
      who are in the aspect of <span class="key-term">orlah</span>, the aspect of falsehood, and
      raise him to the holiness of Israel, who are in the aspect of truth &mdash; this is
      literally an act of judgment, which expels falsehood and clarifies truth. And all of this
      is accomplished through three, who are comprised of the three aspects above, through whom
      all is included in the aspect of all being one &mdash; and through this the
      <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span> is entirely nullified, one ascends from
      impurity to purity, and the convert merits thereby to enter the holiness of Israel,
      as above.
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 12 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">12</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Birchas Kohanim</span> [the Priestly
      Blessing]. For the Kohanim are in the aspect of right, which is the aspect of pre-creation,
      as above &mdash; and from there all blessings are drawn, for the primary grip of the curse
      is only in the aspect of post-creation, as above. And therefore Aharon the Kohen would wave
      all the Levites &mdash; for the Levites are in the aspect of purity, the aspect of
      post-creation, from which a grip can descend to the aspect of many calculations, which is
      the <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span>, etc. Therefore the Kohen was required to
      wave the Levites, so that post-creation be included within pre-creation in the aspect of
      all being one &mdash; to nullify the grip of the <span class="key-term">Sitrah Achara</span>,
      whose grip is due to distance from oneness, as above.
    </p>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of the blessing that is mentioned in the holy Zohar: that before
      the count they would bless Israel, and similarly afterward, as above. For the count is in
      the aspect of post-creation from which their grip descends, as above &mdash; therefore
      they required the Priestly Blessing before and after, so that they be included within the
      aspect of pre-creation where the blessing is found, so that the curse that grips the count
      &mdash; the aspect of post-creation, as above &mdash; not have power, God forbid. For this
      is why they were required to give a half-shekel per head, etc., as above. And therefore
      <span class="key-term">Birchas Kohanim</span> is threefold, as above.
    </p>
  </div>
  <hr class="section-divider">

  <!-- SECTION 13 -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">13</div>
    </div>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of Shavuos, on which the Torah was given &mdash; after they counted
      the days of the <span class="key-term">S&rsquo;firah</span> through which they were purified
      from the filth of Egypt, from the aspect of slave, the aspect of
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span>, the aspect of falsehood, etc., as above &mdash; and
      afterwards they merit to receive the Torah on Shavuos, which is the Torah of truth, through
      which all worlds are connected and post-creation is included within pre-creation. For the
      primary realization of this aspect is accomplished through the Torah of truth. And therefore
      the entire Torah is in the threefold aspect, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said
      <span class="verse-source">((Shabbos 88a))</span>:
      <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;B&rsquo;rich Rachmana d&rsquo;yahiv lan oraisa t&rsquo;li&rsquo;ta&rsquo;ah
      al y&rsquo;dai t&rsquo;li&rsquo;ta&rsquo;i b&rsquo;yom t&rsquo;li&rsquo;ta&rsquo;i
      b&rsquo;yarcha t&rsquo;li&rsquo;ta&rsquo;i&rdquo;</span> [Blessed is the Merciful One who
      gave us the threefold Torah through the threefold one [Moshe, the third of his mother&rsquo;s
      children], on the third day, in the third month]. For the Torah is the aspect of truth,
      the aspect of peace, which comprises the three aspects above through which post-creation
      is included within pre-creation &mdash; which is the purpose of all creation, and for this
      the world was created, as is known. And this is accomplished through the three aspects above.
    </p>
    <p>
      And this is the aspect of
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;al sh&rsquo;loshah d&rsquo;varim ha-olam omaid:
      al ha-din v&rsquo;al ha-emes v&rsquo;al ha-shalom&rdquo;</em></span>
      [&ldquo;Upon three things the world stands: upon judgment, upon truth, and upon peace&rdquo;]
      <span class="verse-source">((Avos))</span>, as it is written:
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;emes u-mishpat shalom shif&rsquo;tu b&rsquo;sha&rsquo;areicaim&rdquo;</em></span>
      [&ldquo;truth and the judgment of peace, judge in your gates&rdquo;]. For these three are
      one aspect, and each one is comprised of three aspects, and all of them together are the
      three aspects above which are the sustaining of the world &mdash; for the primary sustaining
      of the world is when post-creation is included within pre-creation in the aspect of all
      being one, as above. That is the ultimate purpose of all creation, and for this the world
      was created, as is known. And this is accomplished through the three aspects above:
      through din and mishpat [judgment] &mdash; through which, by ruling true judgment, falsehood
      is subdued and truth is clarified, and post-creation is included within pre-creation, as
      above; through emes [truth] &mdash; for all depends upon truth, through which His blessed
      hashgachah rests upon us, and through which all is included within the aspect of all being
      one, as above; and through shalom [peace] &mdash; which is the aspect of the decisive one
      that makes peace between opposites, between right and left, for peace connects all and the
      left is included within the right, post-creation within pre-creation. And this is the
      aspect of <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;Hashem yivaraich es amo va-shalom&rdquo;</em></span>
      [&ldquo;God shall bless His people with peace&rdquo;] <span class="verse-source">((Tehillim 29))</span>
      &mdash; for peace is the vessel that holds blessing, for the primary blessings that are
      drawn from the aspect of pre-creation, where the source of blessing is, cannot be drawn
      down below to post-creation except through peace which connects all and post-creation is
      included within pre-creation, and then blessing is drawn from the source of blessing to all
      of creation. And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Birchas Kohanim</span>, which
      concludes with peace, and their blessing also ends with <em>shalom</em> [&ldquo;place
      peace&rdquo;] &mdash; for the primary blessing is drawn to creation through being included
      within pre-creation, which is the aspect of peace, as above. For the blessing is to be
      saved from and to subdue the curse that grips the aspect of post-creation, and through
      post-creation being included within the aspect of pre-creation in the aspect of all being
      one and entirely good, all curses are nullified at their root and all blessings and all
      goodness are drawn to all of creation. And this is the aspect of
      <span class="verse-quote"><em>&ldquo;Hashem yivaraich es amo va-shalom&rdquo;</em></span>,
      as above.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="summary-box">
    <h4>Translator&rsquo;s Note</h4>
    <p>
      This halachah traces a single luminous thread through many halachic topics: the mitzvah of
      circumcising a slave, the prohibition against emancipating him, the slave&rsquo;s obligation
      in women&rsquo;s mitzvos, S&rsquo;firas ha-Omer, the half-shekel, immersion, a court of
      three, Birchas Kohanim, and Shavuos. The thread is the kabbalistic concept of
      <em>post-creation being included within pre-creation</em> &mdash;
      <span class="key-term">achar ha-b&rsquo;riah nichlal b&rsquo;kodem ha-b&rsquo;riah</span>.
      The slave (<span class="key-term">eved</span>) represents the aspect of the left, of
      number, of falsehood, of distance from oneness. Milah removes the
      <span class="key-term">orlah</span> which is the grip of falsehood at its root, making it
      possible for the slave to be subsumed within the son &mdash; for the left to be gathered
      into the right. Every mitzvah discussed here performs, on its own plane, the same cosmic
      act: drawing the multiplicity of post-creation back to the pure unity that preceded it.
    </p>
  </div>

</div>

  </div>
